# Line-ending policy for the codelisperer monorepo.
#
# Every text file is LF in the repo AND in every working tree, on every OS.
# SBCL compiles the working-tree files directly, and a CRLF turns a FORMAT
# ~<newline> continuation into an illegal ~<Return> directive -- surfaced as a
# compile-time "macroexpansion" error. Forcing LF on checkout makes the build
# identical on Linux/macOS/Windows and immunizes against core.autocrlf.
#
# Source ALSO avoids FORMAT ~<newline> continuations entirely, so that a stray CRLF from
# a zip download or a misconfigured editor -- a tree that did not arrive through
# `git checkout', where the rule above cannot reach -- cannot break the build either.
# That was not true until #146: 76 continuations in 18 files were folded onto one line
# each, and scripts/check-format-continuations.lisp, which the gate runs, fails on any
# string literal that has one.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts are the deliberate exception -- they want CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never normalize.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.dylib binary
*.so    binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
